<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1990</h1><p class="ref-lede">1990 in world history: 27 events, 13 deaths, 2 works, 2 states founded and 5 that came to an end. 201 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1986">1986</a><a href="/years/1987">1987</a><a href="/years/1988">1988</a><a href="/years/1989">1989</a><a href="/years/1990" aria-current="page">1990</a><a href="/years/1991">1991</a><a href="/years/1992">1992</a><a href="/years/1993">1993</a><a href="/years/1994">1994</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/moscow" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moscow.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-31">31 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">McDonald's opens in Moscow</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The first McDonald's in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> opened on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-pushkin">Pushkin</a> Square, serving about 30,000 people on its first day. Queues stretched for hours as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> drew to a close.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-2">2 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">F. W. de Klerk lifts the ban on the ANC</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Opening parliament in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-town">Cape Town</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s President legalised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-national-congress">African National Congress</a> and other banned groups and announced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a>'s release. Negotiations to end apartheid followed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-7">7 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Communist Party agrees to give up its monopoly on power</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Central Committee accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-gorbachev">Mikhail Gorbachev</a>'s proposal to end the party's constitutional leading role. The change opened the way to multi-party politics in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-11">11 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nelson Mandela walks free after 27 years in prison</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Mandela left Victor Verster Prison near Paarl hand in hand with his wife Winnie, watched by millions on television. Four years later he was elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s first Black president.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-18">18 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">East Germany holds its first free elections</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">East Germans voted in their first free parliamentary elections. The conservative Alliance for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> won, opening the way to rapid reunification with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a> in October.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-24">24 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Space shuttle Discovery launches the Hubble Space Telescope</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Hubble was carried into orbit by Discovery and deployed the next day. A flaw in its mirror was corrected in 1993, after which it transformed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-astronomy">astronomy</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-2">2 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Iraq invades Kuwait</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein">Saddam Hussein</a>'s forces overran Kuwait in a matter of hours. A US-led coalition expelled them in early 1991, though Saddam remained in power.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-3">3 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Germany is reunified</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-germany">German Democratic Republic</a> acceded to the Federal Republic, reuniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> 45 years after its division. The peaceful merger, less than a year after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-wall">Berlin Wall</a> opened, marked the close of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-1">1 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Tunnellers from Britain and France meet under the Channel</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">British and French workers broke through the last wall of rock and shook hands beneath the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">English Channel</a>. The tunnel opened in 1994, linking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to the Continent by rail.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/1990-peoples-movement" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/1990-peoples-movement.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/1990-peoples-movement">1990 People's Movement</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The 1990 People's Movement, or Jana Andolan, was a campaign of mass protests and strikes in Nepal from February to April 1990, led by the banned Nepali Congress and an alliance of leftist parties.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/oka-crisis" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oka-crisis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Crisis</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/oka-crisis">Oka crisis</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Oka crisis was a 78-day armed stand-off in 1990 between Mohawk protesters and the Quebec police and Canadian army near the town of Oka, west of Montreal.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/bulgarian-round-table">Bulgarian Round Table</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Bulgarian Round Table was a series of talks in early 1990 between the Bulgarian Communist Party, newly renamed the Socialist Party, and the opposition Union of Democratic Forces.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/german-reunification">German reunification</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">German reunification was the process by which the German Democratic Republic (East Germany) joined the Federal Republic of Germany (West Germany) on 3 October 1990, ending the division of the country that had lasted since 1949.</p></div></li></ol></section>
